{{!
    @template local_vektradiscuss/transcript_links

    The student's own transcripts, one per closed session (REQ-088): a download link when Vektra has it,
    a status sentence otherwise. The link goes to transcript.php, which streams the file as a download.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * uniqid - unique id prefix
    * transcriptsheading - list heading
    * transcripts - list of {n, url (null when not downloadable), text}

    Example context (json):
    {
        "uniqid": "local-vektradiscuss-12",
        "transcriptsheading": "Your transcripts",
        "transcripts": [
            {"n": 1, "url": "https://moodle.example.org/local/vektradiscuss/transcript.php?cmid=12&tid=t-1&n=1&sesskey=x", "text": "Transcript of session 1 (download)"},
            {"n": 2, "url": null, "text": "Transcript of session 2: not available at the moment."}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="local-vektradiscuss-transcripts mt-2">
    <h4 class="h6" id="{{uniqid}}-transcripts">{{transcriptsheading}}</h4>
    <ul class="mb-2" aria-labelledby="{{uniqid}}-transcripts">
        {{#transcripts}}
            <li>
                {{#url}}<a href="{{url}}" data-region="local_vektradiscuss-transcript" data-n="{{n}}">{{text}}</a>{{/url}}
                {{^url}}<span data-region="local_vektradiscuss-transcript" data-n="{{n}}">{{text}}</span>{{/url}}
            </li>
        {{/transcripts}}
    </ul>
</div>
